A||||6||theogre||Interesting: 87-88 DIS 4 ECM Fan Control||||3||
Z||000000||theogre||05-04-2001||08:36 PM||||I've been working on some things with these fans the last few days...<P>What I've found is that 87-88 DIS 4's ECM control for the fan is activating at about 225F. It shuts off when the temp drops beloww 211F. This appears to apply to All 2.5l DIS 4's. This is much better than the 235 that the majority of Fiero's activate at with engine switches.<P>A. Do you own a 87-88 DIS 4?<BR>B. Do you have an ECM scanner, or access to one?<P>If you can answer yes to both those questions...<P>WITH THE A/C OFF!<P>Please hook up you scanner and watch the Coolant Temp sensor in real time. Let the car idle untill you hear the fan activate. Pleace record the PROM ID number and the fan activation temperature in this thread.<P>For those With Out a scanner that would like to test this... 225 Is a little above the 220 mark on the dash gauge. The ECM should start the fan before the dash gauge reaches the next unlabeled mark. <P>------------------<BR><I><B>Screamin Yellow Zonkers... If it's Screamin and Yellow, I ain't eatin it.</B></I>||||reg||3
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||05-09-2001||01:43 AM||||OK, so I lied! <BR>Ran 2 (not 1) '88's today and both are 5-speeds. Prom ID's both the same as well as data, cut in @ 226 and out @ 210.<BR>I'll get to the '87's tomorrow and relay those as well.<BR>They should be slightly different I'd guess since one is an automatic.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||05-09-2001||08:52 PM||||The automatic will have a diferent ID but should have the same activation temps.  (I'd like those ID's just for reference.)<BR>I've tested one out of a grand am and got the same numbers. (It's the chip I happen to have in when I thought to test it. I'm using alternate chips to diagnose a ping problem referenced in a TSB. $60 is too much to get the "fix" chip from GM.) <P>Either way, This is allot better than 235 that most of the old block switch rigs are on. 225 is a little warm but won't hurt anything.||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroJoe||05-10-2001||10:25 AM||||Right now, my 87 DIS 4 wont get above the first labeled mark on the gauge (180 stat), but I do not remember the fan ever coming on before I changed it.  The gauge would read about as hot as you described, but no fan would come on with the AC off.  <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||05-10-2001||07:49 PM||||Joe,<P>If the fan and cooling system are working right.... The fan will only come on in heavy, slow, traffic or when you leave it idle awhile in hot weather. Conditions when there is just no air moving w/o it.<P>Also, You often can't hear it clearly when you are inside the car or near the back of the car with the motor running. I had to open the hood durring my test so I could see the thing.||||reg||1
Z||000005||maryjane||05-10-2001||09:03 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by theogre:<BR><B>Joe,<P>If the fan and cooling system are working right.... The fan will only come on in heavy, slow, traffic or when you leave it idle awhile in hot weather. Conditions when there is just no air moving w/o it.<P>Also, You often can't hear it clearly when you are inside the car or near the back of the car with the motor running. I had to open the hood durring my test so I could see the thing.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Just wonderin? Would it be worth the effort to wire in a small indicator lamp to let you know when fan is running or not? Guess you can always tell by temp gauge but fan is not always overtemp culprit.<BR>Don & Jane||||reg||5
Z||000006||FieroJoe||05-11-2001||07:51 AM||||That would be a good idea if you were really concerned about your engine temp.  If you sit in traffic alot and in hot weather, it may be some use to you.  While you were at running an indicator lamp, you might also want to run a switch so you could manually turn on the fan anytime you wanted to, just so you could start cooling your engine before the ECM says to.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
